          deckDescription: 'Thirty-two-card Hungarian deck (Magyar Kártya), also known as Seasons or William Tell deck. Four German suits with eight ranks per suit (7, 8, 9, 10, Under, Over, King, Ace). Used for point-trick and meld scoring; total 161 card points plus last trick bonus.',
          suitDescription: "Four German suits: Acorns (makk), Leaves (zöld), Hearts (piros), and Gourds (tök). In Hungarian/William Tell decks the Aces show seasonal imagery and the knaves (Over and Under) depict characters from Schiller's William Tell.",
          rankDescription: 'Eight ranks per suit in sequence order (high to low): Ace, King, Over (knave), Under (knave), Ten, Nine, Eight, Seven. Trick order in trumps differs: Over highest then Nine, Ace, Ten, King, Under, Eight, Seven. Plain suits: Ace, Ten, King, Over, Under, Nine, Eight, Seven.',
